# City page layout (locked)

Lincoln (`estados/nebraska/lincoln.html` + `en/states/nebraska/lincoln.html`) is the **canonical city page**. Omaha and every new city use this format. Do not invent a new section order, chart style, or calculator.

Do not bring back Omaha’s old source/price/notes table or the static $10,000 premium grid.

## Section order (do not reorder)

1. Local photo hero — **no prices or premiums** in the H1 or bullets
2. Breadcrumb (state / city)
3. What final expense insurance is
4. Funeral-home **packages**, cheapest to most expensive, with estimator-field descriptions under each name, then the source line **and** the comparison legal note (`funeralHomeCompareNote` in `lib/company-compare-disclaimer.js`)
5. What changes from one home to another (analysis cards)
6. The burial plot is a **separate bill**, then where to call, then resale ads
7. Calculator: age, sex, smoker → appointed-company monthly premium
8. Metro towns
9. License for **this page’s state only** (full roster stays on licencias/licenses)
10. FAQs
11. Navy quote band

## Locked copy (use these wordings)

- Hero plot bullet EN: `The burial plot is a separate cemetery bill, with resale listings that often cost less.`
- Hero plot bullet ES: `El lote es una factura aparte del cementerio, con anuncios de reventa que suelen costar menos.`
- Metro: official quotes are **by phone** (no walk-in office). Do not add WhatsApp or online as the official quote path.
- Analysis card 2 heading EN: `The same package name does not include the same items`
- Analysis card 2 heading ES: `El mismo nombre de paquete no incluye lo mismo`
- Do not write “cart” / “carrito” in that heading.

## Package chart (required)

- Three **local funeral homes** plus the estimator column.
- Every home must **bury and cremate**, and must publish a **complete first-party GPL or package list** (the home’s own site or PDF). No Funeralocity figures in named-home columns.
- Every cell has a dollar amount. Do not use cremation-only homes that leave burial cells blank.
- Package **row** order, cheapest to most expensive: direct cremation → immediate burial → cremation with memorial → traditional funeral with visitation.
- Source line under the table names each GPL’s effective date. Then the comparison legal note. Do not invent a shorter substitute.

## Calculator (required)

Lives in `scripts/city-guide-html.js` + `js/city-guide.js`. Do not rebuild it.

- Vault checkbox includes the locked why-text (`vaultWhy`): most cemeteries require a vault for ground burial so the grave does not sink; it is almost never in the funeral-home package.
- Hide the vault block unless the service is immediate burial or traditional funeral.
- Hide the extra-casket checkbox when that home’s package already includes a casket (`homeIncludesCasket`).

## Builders

- Data: `scripts/city-guides/{slug}.js` (copy Lincoln; fill local homes, packages, cemeteries)
- Template: `scripts/city-guide-html.js`
- Legal note: `lib/company-compare-disclaimer.js`
- Shell: `scripts/render-city-coverage-pages.js` — add the city to `CITIES`; omit `layout` or set `layout: "guide"`
- JS: `js/city-guide.js` + `data/{slug}-plot-resales.json`
- CSS: `.sc-city-guide` in `css/state-coverage.css` — do not scope new styles only to one city
- Then `npm run build:city-pages`. Mirror ES + EN. Spanish indexable; English `noindex`.

## Do not

- Put costs in the hero
- Add a comparable-funeral “added up” row, or an estimator line-item grid with empty cells
- List the four licensed states, Iowa, or “based in Lincoln” on the city page body
- Use Julie’s first name in body copy (agency name only)
- Hand-edit the generated HTML; change the builder and rebuild
- Omit the comparison legal note under the funeral-home package table
- Fill a home column from Funeralocity
- Invent unpublished burial packages
- Skip the vault explanation, or show the vault checkbox on cremation
